From bec8264a560e8c796b577f02da281c618a7f8d2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <arena-agent@local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:07:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Start a retry from an empty timeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A report from a desktop arrived reading setupSeconds: 13 with a timeline whose
first entry was at +118.8s. begin() reset setupStartedAt but left events in
place, so a retry appended to the previous attempt's list and the timeline —
which measures from events[0] — was anchored to the attempt before it. Every
offset in that report was wrong.

begin() now starts from an empty timeline.

It also keeps the failure reason. A retry used to clear error, so the one piece
of evidence about the attempt that had just died was erased by the act of
trying again, and "the status line disappeared on its own" was left with
nothing behind it. It now moves into lastError and the report prints it as
previousAttemptFailed.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
